<title>NETHERLANDS: Italy will meet EMU criteria in 1997 - Dini.</title>
<headline>Italy will meet EMU criteria in 1997 - Dini.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy will meet tough criteria in 1997 for aspirant founder members of the European single currency, but does not know if France will do likewise, Italian Foreign Minister Lamberto Dini said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Italy will meet the criteria, we don't know about France,&quot; Dini told reporters.</p>
<p>Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi added that Italy would need no flexible interpretation of the Maastricht treaty to win membership of European economic and monetary union at its start in 1999.</p>
</text>
